course: dictionary
lesson: 4285
title: Greengrocer and the greengrocer's apostrophe
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A greengrocer is a person who sells fresh fruit and vegetables in a shop. The shop itself is also called the greengrocer's, so the word can mean the person or the place. «The greengrocer's is open until six o'clock.» Here the greengrocer's is the shop.
explain: Notice the clue words around the word. Fresh fruit, vegetables and a shop tell you what a greengrocer is, even if you have never heard the word before. Try the swap check: put «shop that sells fruit and vegetables» in place of greengrocer's, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words are used as jokes. «A wrong apostrophe in a plural is so common on shop signs («apple's 50p») that it has a nickname, the greengrocer's apostrophe.» The name is a joke. It does not mean that greengrocers make more mistakes than anyone else.
fact: A greengrocer sells fresh fruit and vegetables.
fact: The greengrocer's can mean the shop as well as the person who runs it.
fact: A plural means more than one, like apples or bananas.
fact: The greengrocer's apostrophe is a joke name for a wrong apostrophe in a plural, such as «Banana's 30p».
fact: In a plural, you usually do not need an apostrophe: «Bananas 30p» is correct.
exercise: What is a greengrocer? | *A person who sells fresh fruit and vegetables in a shop | A person who fixes cars | A person who sells clothes | A farmer who grows wheat in a field
exercise: «The greengrocer's apostrophe is the name for a wrong apostrophe in a plural.» What is the greengrocer's apostrophe? | A correct apostrophe in a possessive | A kind of fruit | *A wrong apostrophe in a plural, like «Banana's 30p» | A shop sign with no words
exercise: «Mum bought apples by the kilo from the greengrocer's.» Which word is the name of a shop? | bought | kilo | apples | *greengrocer's
test: «The greengrocer's is closed on Sundays.» What does greengrocer's mean here? | A kind of vegetable | A wrong apostrophe | *The shop itself | A person who grows bananas
test: Which shop sign has a wrong plural with an apostrophe? | *Banana's 30p | Bananas 30p | Pears 40p | Apples 50p
exam: A greengrocer sells apples at £2 a kilo. How much do 3 kilos cost? | *£6 | £9 | £5 | £8
